# FDIC Banking Risk ML Pipeline

[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](LICENSE)
[![Python 3.10+](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.10+-blue.svg)](https://www.python.org/downloads/)
[![CI](https://github.com/philiprybkin/fdic-ml-pipeline/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/philiprybkin/fdic-ml-pipeline/actions/workflows/ci.yml)

A local-first machine learning pipeline for FDIC banking data. Engineers risk features from regulatory CSVs, runs clustering and multi-method synopsis analysis, and produces reproducible artifacts and portfolio-ready reports.

## Why This Project

FDIC call-report data contains rich signals about bank capitalization, profitability, and credit stress. This project turns raw CSV exports into:

- **Risk segmentation** via unsupervised clustering (KMeans with silhouette-based model selection)
- **Structural diagnostics** via PCA, anomaly detection, and correlation mining
- **Interpretable supervised models** when a label column is available (logistic regression, elastic net, shallow decision tree)

Designed as a portfolio project demonstrating end-to-end data science workflow: ingestion, feature engineering, ML, artifact generation, and stakeholder reporting.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  CSV[FDIC CSVs] --> Merge[Merge by CERT]
  Merge --> Features[Feature Engineering]
  Features --> Filter[Outlier Filtering]
  Filter --> Clustering[KMeans Clustering]
  Filter --> Synopsis[PCA + Anomaly + Correlations]
  Filter --> Supervised[Interpretable Models]
  Clustering --> Artifacts[backend/artifacts/]
  Synopsis --> Artifacts
  Supervised --> Artifacts
  Artifacts --> Reports[reports/primary/]
```

See [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) for module-level details.

## Quick Start (5 minutes)

```bash
git clone https://github.com/philiprybkin/fdic-ml-pipeline.git
cd fdic-ml-pipeline
python3 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .

# Run demo on bundled sample data (150 institutions)
make run-sample
```

Or manually:

```bash
fdic-ml --config backend/configs/sample.json --mode both
fdic-ml --generate-synopsis-report --output-dir backend/artifacts --reports-dir reports/primary
```

## Full Data Setup

The repository does **not** include full FDIC datasets (~80 MB). See [DATA.md](DATA.md) for:

- Required CSV files and columns
- Where to obtain FDIC data
- Local folder setup (`data/raw/fdic/`)

## Project Layout

```
backend/                  # Pipeline code, tests, configs, sample data
  src/fdic_ml_pipeline/   # Core ML modules
  tests/                  # Unit tests
  configs/                # Run configurations
  data/sample/            # Bundled demo dataset (150 rows)
  artifacts/              # Runtime outputs (gitignored)

reports/                  # Human-readable outputs
  primary/                # Portfolio-ready reports (start here)
  secondary/              # Supporting diagnostics (markdown only)
```

## ML Methods

| Track | Method | Output |
|-------|--------|--------|
| Clustering | KMeans + silhouette selection | Risk segments, cluster profiles |
| Synopsis | PCA, Isolation Forest, correlation pairs | Structural diagnostics |
| Supervised | Logistic (L2/elastic net), shallow decision tree | Predictions + feature explanations |

## Example Results

From a full run on 4,388 FDIC institutions (2025-09-30 snapshot):

- **Best k:** 2 clusters, silhouette **0.8269**
- **Segmentation:** 23 institutions (0.6%) in stressed tail, 4,121 (99.4%) in core
- **PCA:** top 3 components explain **80%** of variance

See [reports/primary/GOLDEN_REPORT_2026-05-07.md](reports/primary/GOLDEN_REPORT_2026-05-07.md) for a complete validated report.

## Tests

```bash
make test
# or
python -m unittest discover -s backend/tests -v
```

## Limitations

- **No label column** in current dataset — supervised mode requires a target (e.g., `FAILED`)
- **Cross-sectional** — not time-series validated; random train/test split (temporal backtesting planned)
- **Anomaly calibration** — IsolationForest `contamination="auto"` may over-flag; explicit tuning recommended
- **Not causal** — clustering identifies structure, not predictive outcomes

## Roadmap

- [ ] Add supervised label dataset (failure/event flags)
- [ ] Time-based rolling backtests
- [ ] Data quality gates and row-retention diagnostics
- [ ] Anomaly contamination configuration
- [ ] Automated golden report generation from pipeline runs

